---
name: abandoned_walks
description: >
  The dither damper (issue #933), appended to a live decide observation.
  Rendered by cognition.abandoned_walks_block() and folded into
  observe_and_decide's observation when the step loop threads a SimClock and
  the agent abandoned a cross-building walk within the last
  ABANDONED_LEG_WINDOW_MIN sim-minutes with nothing new involving that
  building since. #916 fixed the mechanical mid-walk retarget; #878
  candidate 1 then showed the behavioral layer can still alternate
  "legitimate" decides -- 12 cross-building retargets and 238 abandoned-leg
  minutes in one afternoon, a clean 5-cycle Houston <-> Irvine ping-pong
  among them, with no plan memory or conversation justifying any leg. This
  is a discouragement, not a hard block: the model may still travel back,
  but it is asked to state the new reason -- the same override shape the
  precondition-failure feedback gives a blocked action. Which legs qualify
  (the decay window, the new-memory justification, the current scheduled
  stop's exemption) is computed in Python -- it is data; only the wording
  lives here. The deterministic mock reads only the observation's first
  line, so this can never change a mock decision.
inputs:
  legs:
    type: string
    description: >
      Pre-joined "<building> (<N> min ago)" fragments, most recently
      abandoned first ("just now" under a minute), e.g. "Houston Hall
      (12 min ago) and Irvine Auditorium (30 min ago)".
  plural:
    type: boolean
    description: True when more than one abandoned leg is listed.
sample:
  legs: "Houston Hall (12 min ago)"
  plural: false
---
You recently abandoned {% if plural %}walks{% else %}a walk{% endif %} to {{ legs }} without doing anything there, and nothing new has come up about {% if plural %}those places{% else %}that place{% endif %} since. Do not travel back there without a new reason you can state -- walking back and forth wastes the day.
